Audio + shared helper: an apps-SMMU stage-1 context of our own (new bsd/dev/negroni_smmu_s1.c) for the ADSP
stream 0x1801: the speaker ring anywhere in RAM, mapped at IOVA 0x10000000 (Android qcom,msm-audio-ion pool), given
to the ADSP as IOVA | 1 << 32 (msm_audio_ion.c SID bits). 0243 asked for a ring below 4 GiB: impossible, XNU RAM
starts at 0x840000000. negroniaudio_smmu=0 keeps the old physical path. The helper takes free contexts and SMRs
from the top down (Wi-Fi 0324/0325 from the bottom up), free context = U-Boot CBAR rule (as 0325) + SCTLR.M off + no
S2CR into it, CBAR/CBA2R restored at the end, re-reads each SMR and the CBAR before writing; exported claim lock negroni_smmu_claim_lock (scan to
last write, and teardown) for every SMMU user (Wi-Fi 0325 to take it); map checks the TLB sync;
camera (0317) uses it too. Details: patches/xnu/README-camera.md "0317-0318, 0249", docs/notes.md section 38.

